# No. of Functional Features Included in the Solution

## 1. Introduction

The project includes multiple functional features to implement secure and controlled access to institution records in ServiceNow.

## 2. Functional Features

### 2.1 User Management

Users can be created and configured in ServiceNow for access-control testing.

### 2.2 Role Management

Roles can be created and assigned to users according to the required permissions.

### 2.3 Table Management

A custom table named `u_institution_details` is created to store institution and student-related information.

### 2.4 Field Management

The table contains the required fields, including Student Roll Number, Student Name, Faculty Name, Branch, Email, Phone Number, and Description.

### 2.5 Record Management

Sample records can be created with different branch values for testing the access-control rules.

### 2.6 READ Access Control

The READ ACL controls whether users can view the applicable records.

### 2.7 CREATE Access Control

The CREATE ACL controls whether users can create new records.

### 2.8 WRITE Access Control

The WRITE ACL controls whether users can modify existing records.

### 2.9 DELETE Access Control

The DELETE ACL controls whether users can delete records.

### 2.10 Branch-Based Restriction

The Branch field is used as part of the configured record-access conditions.

The project uses:

* ECE
* EEE
* CSE

### 2.11 Administrator Access

Administrators have the required access to manage the system and its security configuration.

### 2.12 Access Testing

The configured ACLs are tested using different users, roles, operations, and record conditions.

## 3. Feature Summary

The solution includes **12 major functional features** covering user management, role management, data management, CRUD access control, branch-based restriction, administrator access, and testing.

## 4. Expected Result

These features work together to provide a structured and controlled record-access system in ServiceNow.
